## 7. KV cache (derived, checked against three published figures)

Every layer stores keys and values for {{ C.kv_heads }} heads of {{ C.head_dim }}:
{{ n(KV.elements_per_token_per_layer) }} values per token per layer.

| per token | BF16 | MXFP8 | NVFP4-style |
|---|---|---|---|
| one layer | {{ n(KV.bytes_per_token_per_layer.bf16) }} B | {{ n(KV.bytes_per_token_per_layer.mxfp8) }} B | {{ n(KV.bytes_per_token_per_layer.nvfp4_style) }} B |
| the {{ C.full_layers }} full-attention layers | {{ n(KV.target_full_bytes_per_token.bf16) }} B | {{ n(KV.target_full_bytes_per_token.mxfp8) }} B | {{ n(KV.target_full_bytes_per_token.nvfp4_style) }} B |
| at {{ n(KV.max_context) }} tokens | {{ gb(KV.at_max_context_bytes.target_bf16) }} | {{ gb(KV.at_max_context_bytes.target_mxfp8) }} | {{ gb(KV.at_max_context_bytes.target_nvfp4_style) }} |

* **Full-attention ("global") layers** are the only ones whose cache grows with context.
* **Sliding-window ("local") layers** keep the last {{ n(KV.window) }} tokens:
  {{ mb(KV.sliding_bytes_per_request_bf16) }} per request in BF16, whatever the context.
* **The draft** adds {{ C.draft_layers }} full-history layers that stay in BF16
  (`tokenspeed-recipe`): {{ n(KV.draft_full_bytes_per_token_bf16) }} B per token,
  {{ gb(KV.at_max_context_bytes.draft_bf16) }} at full context. With an MXFP8 cache for the target
  model, the draft's cache is the larger of the two.

Cross-checks against published figures (measured, source):

| check | ours | published | source |
|---|---|---|---|
| MXFP8 cache, bytes per token per full layer, per rank at TP4 | {{ n(KV.cross_checks.mxfp8_bytes_per_rank_tp4.ours) }} | {{ n(KV.cross_checks.mxfp8_bytes_per_rank_tp4.published) }} | `{{ KV.cross_checks.mxfp8_bytes_per_rank_tp4.src }}` |
| MXFP8 cache over BF16 cache, draft included | {{ n(KV.cross_checks.mxfp8_over_bf16_with_draft.ours, 3) }} | {{ n(KV.cross_checks.mxfp8_over_bf16_with_draft.published, 2) }} | `{{ KV.cross_checks.mxfp8_over_bf16_with_draft.src }}` |
| KV for one request at full context, BF16 | {{ n(KV.cross_checks.one_request_at_max_context_gib_bf16.ours, 1) }} GiB | {{ n(KV.cross_checks.one_request_at_max_context_gib_bf16.published, 2) }} GiB | `{{ KV.cross_checks.one_request_at_max_context_gib_bf16.src }}` |

The first two agree. **The third does not**: vLLM reserves
{{ x(KV.cross_checks.one_request_at_max_context_gib_bf16.ratio_published_over_ours, 2) }} what our count gives.
We did not find the reason; see section 12.

The "NVFP4-style" column is hypothetical. The announcement mentions an NVFP4 KV-cache variant
(`tml-news`), but the cache the public engines expose is MXFP8 (`sglang-recipe`, `tokenspeed-recipe`).

## 8. Speculative decoding changes the step (napkin)

The checkpoint ships a draft model, and every published speed uses it. One step drafts 7 tokens and
verifies {{ DS.verify_rows }} rows per request (`vllm-recipe`, `sglang-recipe`); {{ CONST.speculation.acceptance_published[0] }} to
{{ CONST.speculation.acceptance_published[1] }} tokens are accepted (`vllm-blog`).

The {{ DS.verify_rows }} rows share the dense weights but route separately. If rows route uniformly and
independently, {{ DS.expert_picks_per_layer }} picks hit {{ n(DS.distinct_experts_per_layer_uniform_independent, 1) }}
distinct experts per layer, and one step reads:

| one speculative step | bytes |
|---|---|
| experts | {{ gb(DS.bytes.experts) }} |
| BF16 attention projections and router | {{ gb(DS.bytes.dense_bf16_attention_and_router) }} |
| draft model | {{ gb(DS.bytes.draft_bf16) }} |
| BF16 output projection | {{ gb(DS.bytes.unembed_bf16) }} |
| **total** | **{{ gb(DS.bytes_total) }}** |

At {{ DS.acceptance_assumed }} accepted tokens that is {{ gb(DS.bytes_per_accepted_token) }} per token,
{{ x(DS.bytes_per_token_vs_no_speculation, 2) }} the bytes of decoding without speculation. **Speculation
does not save memory traffic under independent routing; it saves fixed latency.** Real routing is
correlated between neighbouring tokens, which lowers the expert bytes. We have no Inkling routing
traces, so the routing sweep ([04](04_results.md), section 10) brackets this.

